## 3. TSUTOMU NIHEI

### Style DNA
Silence as compositional strategy. Nihei treats architecture as the real protagonist — human figures are often tiny, dwarfed by impossible megastructures that extend in every direction with brutalist repetition. Heavy shadow, laser-etched linework, long wordless stretches. His images feel like they were captured inside a server farm the size of a continent. Blame! and Biomega are the reference points.

### Locked Template
```
A late-1990s brutalist cyberpunk manga image of a [CHARACTER/HOOK], In the style of Tsutomu Nihei, [SCENE, SCALE, ARCHITECTURE, FIGURE DETAILS], impossible architectural scale, near-silent composition, heavy shadow and laser-etched linework, brutalist concrete megastructure
```

### Anchor Phrases (locked)
1. `A late-1990s brutalist cyberpunk manga image of a`
2. `In the style of Tsutomu Nihei`
3. `impossible architectural scale, near-silent composition, heavy shadow and laser-etched linework, brutalist concrete megastructure`

### Signature Visual Keywords
impossible vertical scale, endless concrete corridors, graviton beam discharge, cable-threaded ceilings kilometers above, shadow pools, laser-etched line precision, near-empty compositions, figures as small as rivets in frame, biomechanical safeguards, Silicon Creature anatomy, helmeted builders, narrow catwalks over voids, pressure-door hydraulics, exposed rebar the size of trees

### Typical Subjects & Archetypes
lone wanderer with a gun bigger than sense, biomechanical guardians, silicon parasites, tribal human remnants, construction entities, corrupted safeguards, near-immortal travelers searching for a net terminal gene

### Environments & Worlds
megastructures extending beyond the horizon, concrete corridors kilometers long, vertical elevator shafts that drop out of frame, industrial sectors lit by single distant light sources, collapsed levels with biological overgrowth, fusion reactor chambers, catwalks over unfathomable drops, gravity-well chambers

### Materials & Textures
raw concrete, rusted rebar, hardened polymer armor, biomechanical tendon, crystallized silicate, graviton burn scars, matte black body armor, corroded steel grating, dust clouds in shafts of light

### Emotional Register
cosmic loneliness; the existential vertigo of scale; patience worn to silence; the serenity of a figure who has been walking for a thousand years and will keep walking; dread rendered as emptiness rather than action

### Prompt Construction Priorities
1. Lead with scale — how small is the figure, how big is the space
2. Describe the architecture as if it extends beyond what can be shown
3. Human or semi-human figure is incidental to the space
4. One weapon or object rendered with technical clarity
5. Close with a silence or a single light source that makes the emptiness legible

### Example Prompts

```
A late-1990s brutalist cyberpunk manga image of a silent wanderer standing on a catwalk inside a megastructure column so wide the opposite wall is not visible, In the style of Tsutomu Nihei, tiny figure in matte black armor with an oversized graviton weapon slung across his back rendered in crisp technical detail, the catwalk a thin strand of rusted grating crossing a shaft that drops into blackness below and rises into blackness above, a single distant floodlight catching dust motes thirty stories overhead, concrete walls textured with kilometers of rebar and tool marks receding to vanishing points in every direction, no horizon no sky no ground only structure, impossible architectural scale, near-silent composition, heavy shadow and laser-etched linework, brutalist concrete megastructure
```

```
A late-1990s brutalist cyberpunk manga image of a biomechanical safeguard crouched in an empty chamber the size of a cathedral waiting for intruders that have not arrived for a century, In the style of Tsutomu Nihei, figure armored in overlapping carbon plates with extended mandible-like sensors, single red eye dimmed to standby, surrounded by skeletal remains of previous intruders fused into the concrete floor, cables descending from a ceiling lost in shadow, a thin shaft of light from a breach in the far wall illuminating a single footprint in the dust that is not hers, impossible architectural scale, near-silent composition, heavy shadow and laser-etched linework, brutalist concrete megastructure
```

