## 5. HIROAKI SAMURA

### Style DNA
The preserved graphite sketch as finished art. Samura works in pencil and brush and does not clean up — the construction lines, smudges, and drafting marks are the aesthetic. Combined with sumi-e wash shadows and unconventional compositions, the result reads like a working sketchbook of an Edo-period fight that might or might not have happened. Blade of the Immortal is the reference.

### Locked Template
```
A chanbara ink-and-graphite manga image of a [CHARACTER/HOOK], In the style of Hiroaki Samura, [SCENE, FIGURE, BLADE ACTION, ENVIRONMENT], loose pencil and brush ink, preserved graphite construction lines, Edo-period atmosphere, sumi-e wash shadows
```

### Anchor Phrases (locked)
1. `A chanbara ink-and-graphite manga image of a`
2. `In the style of Hiroaki Samura`
3. `loose pencil and brush ink, preserved graphite construction lines, Edo-period atmosphere, sumi-e wash shadows`

### Signature Visual Keywords
visible construction lines, smudged graphite, wet brush ink, broken contour linework, kinetic smear for motion, realistic facial structure, split-pose blade choreography, blood as dark ink bloom, diagonal slashes, hair rendered in loose brush strokes, fabric folds preserved as rough sketch

### Typical Subjects & Archetypes
ronin, bodyguard samurai, disgraced students, female warriors with specific weapon obsessions, bounty hunters, aging sword masters, mercenary orders, cursed immortals, traveling dojo challengers

### Environments & Worlds
Edo-period roads, teahouse interiors mid-fight, bamboo groves, river crossings at dusk, mountain shrines, plum blossom orchards in wind, inn courtyards at dawn, snow-covered roads with a single set of footprints

### Materials & Textures
graphite smudge, wet brush ink, kimono silk folds, worn leather sandal straps, lacquered scabbards, crow feathers, falling cherry petals, bamboo splinters, blood mist, rope binding, wet road stone

### Emotional Register
the stillness before violence; violence that is over in two seconds and feels longer than the three minutes leading to it; the specific grief of surviving the fight; respect between opponents; the quiet after

### Prompt Construction Priorities
1. Lead with the character's role in the fight or its aftermath
2. Describe the blade or the wound with specificity
3. Keep the environment minimal — one or two grounding details
4. Emphasize texture of render: graphite, smudge, brush
5. Close with an atmospheric detail — weather, falling petals, a stray animal

### Example Prompts

```
A chanbara ink-and-graphite manga image of a female bounty hunter standing in a bamboo grove two seconds after the end of a fight that was never going to end any other way, In the style of Hiroaki Samura, long black hair half-loose from its tie and clinging to the sweat on her jaw, bare-shouldered in a loose indigo kimono now slashed open across the collarbone, a pair of curved blades in her hands held low and angled wide dripping ink-black blood into a loose spiral on the forest floor, three bodies around her in the mid-ground with expressions that have not yet caught up to being dead, shafts of late afternoon sun cutting through the bamboo stalks in diagonal bands, loose pencil and brush ink, preserved graphite construction lines, Edo-period atmosphere, sumi-e wash shadows
```

```
A chanbara ink-and-graphite manga image of an aging sword master meeting his final student on a frozen mountain pass, In the style of Hiroaki Samura, old man in grey travel robes with a single blade sheathed at his hip and a face carved by decades of outliving people, standing twenty paces from a young ronin whose stance is perfect and whose eyes are already accepting this will not go her way, snow falling in wet brush strokes across the whole scene, a crow on a rock between them both of them ignoring, mountain cliff dropping into cloud at the edge of the composition, loose pencil and brush ink, preserved graphite construction lines, Edo-period atmosphere, sumi-e wash shadows
```

