## 6. TAKEHIKO INOUE

### Style DNA
Brush as the only tool. Inoue's Vagabond-era work is closer to traditional sumi-e ink painting than to conventional manga — vast negative space, a single definitive brushstroke doing the work of ten lines, and anatomy rendered with the expressive economy of a master calligrapher. The physicality of bodies — samurai, athletes — is unmatched.

### Locked Template
```
A sumi-e samurai manga image of a [CHARACTER/HOOK], In the style of Takehiko Inoue, [FIGURE, GESTURE, NEGATIVE SPACE, ATMOSPHERE], pure sumi-e brushwork, atmospheric ink wash, minimal linework with expressive anatomy, negative space composition
```

### Anchor Phrases (locked)
1. `A sumi-e samurai manga image of a`
2. `In the style of Takehiko Inoue`
3. `pure sumi-e brushwork, atmospheric ink wash, minimal linework with expressive anatomy, negative space composition`

### Signature Visual Keywords
single-stroke brush lines, vast negative space, ink-splash abstraction, expressive musculature, gestural hair strokes, mid-air suspended motion, wet-on-wet ink bleed, realistic but economical faces, bare backs and shoulders with visible spine, breath visible as a thin wash, grounded bare feet, the weight of a body rendered by a single curve

### Typical Subjects & Archetypes
wandering swordsmen, disciplined disciples, ascetic monks, bare-knuckle travelers, wheelchair athletes, basketball players mid-jump, dueling masters, solitary old warriors at rest, mothers doing ordinary labor with extraordinary grace

### Environments & Worlds
empty dojo floors, mountain roads, temple courtyards at dawn, endless fields under open sky, ink-wash rivers, plum tree branches in wind, snowy duel grounds, rain on wooden verandas, basketball court floors under gymnasium light

### Materials & Textures
ink bleed, bare skin with muscle definition, rough cloth, wooden floor grain, straw sandal weave, sweat, breath mist, light splash of rain, bandaged fists, braided hair

### Emotional Register
presence; the quiet of a person fully inhabiting a moment; the weight of decades of practice; breath; the beauty of a body doing exactly what it was trained to do; stillness as its own language

### Prompt Construction Priorities
1. Lead with the character's state of being, not their role
2. Anchor in one specific physical gesture — the weight of a body, the angle of a shoulder
3. Use negative space aggressively — describe what is NOT in the frame
4. Environment is minimal, atmospheric
5. Close with breath, wind, rain, or silence

### Example Prompts

```
A sumi-e samurai manga image of a lone ronin standing at the end of a narrow wooden bridge waiting for an opponent who may never come, In the style of Takehiko Inoue, bare feet on damp planks, kimono open across the chest showing the rise and fall of one slow breath, a single blade held loose at his side rendered in one long brushstroke, the rest of the composition empty except for a wash of rain across the upper half and the suggestion of water flowing beneath the bridge in three minimal strokes, hair falling across one eye, his expression neither calm nor tense only present, pure sumi-e brushwork, atmospheric ink wash, minimal linework with expressive anatomy, negative space composition
```

