## 7. TAKATO YAMAMOTO

### Style DNA
Heisei-era ero-guro aestheticism. Yamamoto fuses ukiyo-e compositional grammar with Aubrey Beardsley's decorative flat planes and the grotesque-beautiful tradition of Japanese erotic horror. His figures are bound, bleeding, serene. The violence is ornamental. Color palettes pulled from Taisho-era design: deep reds, cream, inky black, gold, pale flesh tones. Everything feels lacquered.

### Locked Template
```
An ero-guro ukiyo-e manga image of a [CHARACTER/HOOK], In the style of Takato Yamamoto, [FIGURE, ORNAMENT, BINDING OR WOUND, DECORATIVE MOTIF], flat decorative planes, Taisho-era color palette, Beardsley-influenced silhouettes, lacquered finish
```

### Anchor Phrases (locked)
1. `An ero-guro ukiyo-e manga image of a`
2. `In the style of Takato Yamamoto`
3. `flat decorative planes, Taisho-era color palette, Beardsley-influenced silhouettes, lacquered finish`

### Signature Visual Keywords
flat planes of color, decorative pattern backgrounds, Beardsley silhouettes, bound wrists, ornamental blood ribbons, lacquered finish, chrysanthemum motifs, cherry blossom scatter, gold ornamental borders, pale skin against ink-black hair, single line mouths, elongated necks, delicate fingers, ropes with traditional shibari knots, serene expressions during suffering, ceremonial kimono patterns, pattern repetition in fabric, isolated bloom-drops of red against cream

### Typical Subjects & Archetypes
bound maidens, young male saints pierced with arrows, ghost brides, decapitated beauties smiling, twin figures mirrored, serpents and butterflies entwined with human forms, lovers united by wound, priests of doubtful gods, Taisho-era schoolgirls with secrets

### Environments & Worlds
traditional Japanese interiors with shoji screens, moonlit gardens, ceremonial chambers, red-lacquered hallways, Taisho-era salons, chrysanthemum fields, ceremonial altars, still pools reflecting ornamental stone lanterns, empty stages

### Materials & Textures
lacquer, silk kimono with printed patterns, hemp rope, cream surfaces, ink-black hair, porcelain skin, blood rendered as decorative red, gold leaf borders, chrysanthemum petals, brass pin ornaments, pearl accents

### Emotional Register
beauty that does not flinch from suffering; serenity during violence; eroticism without urgency; the decorative quality of pain; the sacred in the bound body; elegance as armor

### Prompt Construction Priorities
1. Lead with the figure's ornamental condition — bound, wounded, adorned
2. Emphasize flat decorative composition, not depth
3. Describe the pattern language of the setting — what repeats, what ornaments
4. Color palette and lacquered finish are part of the prompt
5. Close with a decorative detail — a butterfly, a petal, a drop of blood held in place

### Example Prompts

```
An ero-guro ukiyo-e manga image of a young woman bound in ceremonial crimson rope against a folding screen painted with chrysanthemums, In the style of Takato Yamamoto, ink-black hair falling in a single flat plane across one shoulder, pale skin contrasted against the deep red cord wrapped in traditional shibari patterns across her bare arms and ribs, a single bead of red lacquered blood suspended at her collarbone like a jewel, her expression serene almost bored, kimono open at the shoulders revealing decorative sleeves still attached at the wrist, cream background broken by scattered black silhouettes of chrysanthemum blooms, gold leaf border framing the whole composition, flat decorative planes, Taisho-era color palette, Beardsley-influenced silhouettes, lacquered finish
```

```
An ero-guro ukiyo-e manga image of twin sisters sharing a single wound across their joined palms in a moonlit garden pavilion, In the style of Takato Yamamoto, both in identical white kimono with pale plum-pattern borders, mirrored in pose kneeling facing each other, hands pressed together with a single decorative cut drawn between them in three bright red lines, ink-black hair flowing down their backs in flat planes, eyes closed, ornamental silver pins in their hair, moon rendered as a flat cream disc behind a cutout silhouette of a plum branch, flat decorative planes, Taisho-era color palette, Beardsley-influenced silhouettes, lacquered finish
```

