## 8. SHINTARO KAGO

### Style DNA
Matter-of-fact body horror delivered with fashion-illustration clarity. Kago draws the most disturbing transformations imaginable in clean, confident, almost cheerful linework, with backgrounds that look like 1970s consumer graphics. The horror emerges from impossible geometry, fractal body dissections, and the characters' complete lack of alarm.

### Locked Template
```
A surreal fractal body-horror manga image of a [CHARACTER/HOOK], In the style of Shintaro Kago, [SCENE, IMPOSSIBLE TRANSFORMATION, EVERYDAY SETTING, CALM REACTIONS], clean confident linework, matter-of-fact horror composition, fractal body geometry, 1970s consumer graphics clarity
```

### Anchor Phrases (locked)
1. `A surreal fractal body-horror manga image of a`
2. `In the style of Shintaro Kago`
3. `clean confident linework, matter-of-fact horror composition, fractal body geometry, 1970s consumer graphics clarity`

### Signature Visual Keywords
clean precise linework, fashion-editorial faces, fractal body dissection, impossible geometric body horror, characters folding into geometric patterns, bodies as Escher staircases, cheerful background textures, consumer product visual language, 1970s schoolgirl uniforms, ordinary office interiors, everyday salaryman subjects, casual reactions to impossible events, polka dots and pattern wallpaper, commercial poster composition

### Typical Subjects & Archetypes
schoolgirls in pleated uniforms, salarymen on commutes, housewives in kitchens, nurses, office workers, commuters — ordinary Showa-era and early Heisei Japanese citizens experiencing catastrophic transformation with mild curiosity

### Environments & Worlds
subway platforms, classroom interiors, salaryman apartments, supermarket aisles, office cubicles, train car interiors, hospital waiting rooms, public bathhouses, suburban kitchens — rendered flat and ordinary, made horrifying by the geometric violation of the bodies within

### Materials & Textures
clean flat linework, pattern wallpaper, polka dots, formica countertops, pleated skirt fabric, fluorescent lighting, consumer packaging graphics, schoolgirl socks, office carpet, flesh dissected into geometric cross-sections showing impossible interior layers, bone rendered as clean white shape

### Emotional Register
blank affect; the specific comedy of treating body horror as an inconvenience; polite unflappability; the flatness of corporate Japan meeting the infinite; a kind of cheerful dread

### Prompt Construction Priorities
1. Lead with the character as ordinary, specific, boringly employed
2. Introduce an impossible geometric body horror as a matter-of-fact fact of their day
3. The setting should be aggressively ordinary — commute, workplace, home
4. Everyone reacts calmly, including the transformed
5. Close with a mundane detail that refuses to acknowledge the impossibility

### Example Prompts

```
A surreal fractal body-horror manga image of a salaryman whose cross-section becomes visible every time he turns sideways on the morning train, In the style of Shintaro Kago, man in grey suit and thin tie holding a briefcase standing in a packed rush-hour train car, his torso split open as a clean anatomical diagram when seen from the side showing nested layers of organs stacked in impossible geometric repetition like a fractal lunch tray, other passengers in the car completely unbothered one woman reading a book one student napping against the window one older man glancing once then away, fluorescent lighting and polka-dot advertisement posters on the interior walls, clean confident linework, matter-of-fact horror composition, fractal body geometry, 1970s consumer graphics clarity
```

```
A surreal fractal body-horror manga image of a schoolgirl whose body has unfolded into a series of flat thin layers that she is currently ironing on her kitchen table, In the style of Shintaro Kago, young girl in pleated sailor uniform standing barefoot at an ordinary suburban kitchen table methodically ironing stacked thin translucent sheets of herself that still have her face printed on each layer, her remaining partial body standing calmly attending to the task, cheerful polka-dot wallpaper and a calendar on the wall behind her, a rice cooker on the counter, her mother passing through the doorway in an apron saying something about dinner without looking up, clean confident linework, matter-of-fact horror composition, fractal body geometry, 1970s consumer graphics clarity
```

