## 10. TAIYO MATSUMOTO

### Style DNA
Scratchy pen on rough surface, wobbling perspective, childlike faces with adult eyes. Matsumoto's line is deliberately loose — perspective points drift, walls lean, figures are slightly wrong in proportion, and the result is more emotionally precise than any technically clean drawing could be. French bande dessinée influence (Moebius, Jean-Claude Mézières) is heavy. Tekkonkinkreet rooftops, Ping Pong sweat, Sunny abandonment. Urban melancholy.

### Locked Template
```
An independent Japanese urban-melancholy manga image of a [CHARACTER/HOOK], In the style of Taiyo Matsumoto, [SCENE, CHARACTER, URBAN DETAIL, EMOTIONAL BEAT], loose scratchy pen linework, wobbling one-point perspective, French bande dessinée coloring, faded urban palette, childlike melancholy
```

### Anchor Phrases (locked)
1. `An independent Japanese urban-melancholy manga image of a`
2. `In the style of Taiyo Matsumoto`
3. `loose scratchy pen linework, wobbling one-point perspective, French bande dessinée coloring, faded urban palette, childlike melancholy`

### Signature Visual Keywords
loose scratchy pen, hatching that goes slightly wrong, wobbling perspective with drifting vanishing points, childlike figure proportions with adult expressions, Moebius-influenced urban density, rooftops and fire escapes, laundry lines across alleyways, handwritten signage, cats on walls, kids in t-shirts and shorts, sneakers with uneven laces, sweat droplets, scraped knees, faded primary colors, French-BD flat washes, crowded small apartments

### Typical Subjects & Archetypes
street kids, runaways, aging boxers, competitive athletes with something wrong in their head, abandoned siblings, care-home children, neighborhood eccentrics, delivery riders, small-time gangsters with regrets, single mothers, cats who know everyone

### Environments & Worlds
Tokyo rooftops with satellite dishes and laundry, back-alley convenience stores, elementary schoolyards at dusk, small apartments with low ceilings, public bathhouses, table tennis gymnasiums, care home dining rooms, small-town train stations, overpass undersides, basketball half-courts behind schools

### Materials & Textures
scratchy pen, faded t-shirt cotton, scraped sneaker rubber, bandaged hands, sweat, cheap wooden floor, fluorescent lighting in convenience stores, chipped paint on railings, rusted chain-link, cat fur, rice lanterns in small shops

### Emotional Register
melancholy; the particular loneliness of childhood; longing without hope; the beauty of small ordinary scenes witnessed too late; resignation wearing a half-smile; the ache of places you can't go back to

### Prompt Construction Priorities
1. Lead with the character's emotional condition more than their role
2. Render the environment with specific small urban details
3. Perspective should feel slightly off — describe from an angle, not straight-on
4. Include one small grounding detail (a cat, a vending machine, a plastic bag)
5. Close with a weather note or a mood note

### Example Prompts

```
An independent Japanese urban-melancholy manga image of two brothers on a rooftop at dusk eating popsicles they stole from the convenience store below, In the style of Taiyo Matsumoto, older brother maybe twelve in an oversized t-shirt and cargo shorts sitting on the edge of the roof with his legs dangling over the alley, younger brother maybe six leaning against a satellite dish already getting popsicle drip down his wrist, perspective slightly tilted as if the whole roof is listing to one side, laundry lines with other peoples' shirts strung between this building and the next, a skinny cat on a wall watching them without interest, sky faded orange and pink in loose French-BD washes, handwritten kanji signage on the neighboring rooftop water tower, loose scratchy pen linework, wobbling one-point perspective, French bande dessinée coloring, faded urban palette, childlike melancholy
```

```
An independent Japanese urban-melancholy manga image of an aging table tennis coach watching his final student practice alone in an empty gym after closing time, In the style of Taiyo Matsumoto, old man sitting on a folding chair in a sweatshirt two sizes too big nursing a can of coffee from the vending machine, the student a teenage girl in a faded school tracksuit hitting the ball against a folded-up table alone across the gym, fluorescent lights buzzing overhead with one tube flickering, perspective wobbling slightly so the far wall of the gym leans left, sneakers and a half-zipped bag by the door, wooden floor showing years of scuff marks, loose scratchy pen linework, wobbling one-point perspective, French bande dessinée coloring, faded urban palette, childlike melancholy
