## 11. JUNJI ITO

### Style DNA
Hyper-detailed stippling and crosshatching in service of slow-building dread. Ito's horror is patient, domestic, and uncanny — the wrongness accumulates until it becomes undeniable. Influenced by Western horror (Lovecraft) and Japanese folk dread. His faces are either beautiful or wrong; his spirals are the most famous shape in modern horror art. Pure black-and-white ink, no color, no mercy.

### Locked Template
```
A Japanese psychological horror manga image of a [CHARACTER/HOOK], In the style of Junji Ito, [SCENE, WRONGNESS, DOMESTIC OR QUIET SETTING, UNCANNY DETAIL], hyper-detailed stippling and crosshatching, cold dread composition, black-and-white ink rendering, Western horror influence, uncanny stillness
```

### Anchor Phrases (locked)
1. `A Japanese psychological horror manga image of a`
2. `In the style of Junji Ito`
3. `hyper-detailed stippling and crosshatching, cold dread composition, black-and-white ink rendering, Western horror influence, uncanny stillness`

### Signature Visual Keywords
hyper-detailed stippling, dense crosshatching, spiral motifs, impossible hair growth, bodies opening into wrong shapes, pore-level skin rendering, fingernails extending, eyes that are the wrong size or the wrong quantity, mouths too full of teeth, dolls that blink, long-haired women in hallways, small coastal towns with something in the lighthouse, domestic interiors rendered in exhausting detail, no motion lines — everything frozen

### Typical Subjects & Archetypes
teenage girls in school uniforms who notice something first, boyfriends who don't notice anything, elderly fishermen with warnings, parents replaced slowly, beautiful women who are not what they seem, children holding dolls that are children, siblings separated by curses, loners in seaside towns, idealists being consumed by an aesthetic

### Environments & Worlds
seaside Japanese towns with too much fog, school hallways after hours, suburban homes with one room locked, mountain villages where the well is wrong, concrete apartment buildings with one window always lit, beaches at low tide with things exposed, attics, basements, lighthouses, shrines on small islands, hospital corridors

### Materials & Textures
stippled skin, dense hair rendered strand by strand, cold concrete, damp wood, wet hair against skin, porcelain doll faces, fingernails as blades, eyeballs as surfaces, ink pools for shadow, fabric folds rendered with unnatural patience

### Emotional Register
cold dread; the specific horror of domestic wrongness; the patience of a curse; love turning into its own horror; the quiet before you understand; dread that persists after looking away

### Prompt Construction Priorities
1. Lead with the character and the normalcy of their situation
2. Introduce the wrongness as a single specific detail, rendered with excessive clarity
3. Setting should be domestic, small-town, ordinary — horror needs contrast
4. Avoid motion — everything should feel frozen, caught mid-realization
5. Close with an uncanny detail the viewer shouldn't quite notice on first read

### Example Prompts

```
A Japanese psychological horror manga image of a schoolgirl who has just realized her reflection in the classroom window has been turning its head independently for the past hour, In the style of Junji Ito, teenage girl in a sailor uniform seated at a desk by the window after school, classroom empty behind her rendered in exhausting detail down to the dust on the blackboard chalk rail, her own face frozen mid-turn toward the glass, the reflection in the window showing her face already fully turned and smiling back with too many teeth, her hair in the reflection slightly longer than her actual hair, the fluorescent light above stippled into uncanny whiteness, no motion lines, everything held still, hyper-detailed stippling and crosshatching, cold dread composition, black-and-white ink rendering, Western horror influence, uncanny stillness
```

```
A Japanese psychological horror manga image of a young wife who has started noticing that her husband's hair grows an inch every night and that he no longer remembers his mother's name, In the style of Junji Ito, couple in a small traditional Japanese living room at breakfast, husband sitting seiza at a low table with his back to the viewer his black hair now pooling on the tatami around him in rendered strand-by-strand detail, wife kneeling across from him holding a teacup frozen halfway to her mouth, her face a portrait of a woman understanding something one second before she wants to, the sliding door behind him slightly open showing darkness in the next room that is more concentrated than it should be, a framed wedding photograph on the wall in which his face is now facing away, hyper-detailed stippling and crosshatching, cold dread composition, black-and-white ink rendering, Western horror influence, uncanny stillness
```

